<linker>
  <!--
    Preserves every type/member under AnyToneCPS.Models from trimming.

    Real crash found 2026-08-17: EncryptionKeyEntry.EncryptionIdText is a
    genuine public property (see EncryptionKeyEntry.cs), but Desktop's
    NativeAOT publish threw "The type 'EncryptionKeyEntry' does not contain
    a public property named 'EncryptionIdText'" on startup - CommunityToolkit
    .Mvvm's ObservableValidator.ValidateProperty(object, string), called from
    every model's OnXxxTextChanged partial method, is explicitly marked
    RequiresUnreferencedCode because it finds the named property via
    reflection at runtime, and the trimmer stripped that property's metadata
    since nothing else in the app reflects on it by name. Android's own
    NativeAOT publish did not hit this same crash - the two toolchains trim
    differently - but the same crash is latent for any other "*Text"
    validated property (there are dozens, same pattern throughout Models),
    on either platform, the moment execution happens to reach one the
    trimmer decided to strip. A per-property [DynamicDependency] fix (the
    pattern used for MainViewModel.DevForceModelToImage's own reflection)
    doesn't scale here and would silently miss any property added later -
    rooting the whole Models namespace is the general fix.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="AnyToneCPS">
    <type fullname="AnyToneCPS.Models.*" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
